1
00:01:50,345 --> 00:01:52,345


2
00:01:52,449 --> 00:01:56,201
Blinded, Sapphire is carried off by Mephisto,

3
00:01:57,165 --> 00:01:59,401
but Hecate rescues her just in time.

4
00:01:59,425 --> 00:02:00,853
Meanwhile, on Sea Snake Island,

5
00:02:00,878 --> 00:02:03,900
she found the King and Queen had been  turned to stone.

6
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:08,575
Sapphire fell into the sea while trying to save the King and the others,

7
00:02:08,599 --> 00:02:12,321
but was rescued by Pirate Blood.

8
00:02:12,345 --> 00:02:15,340
 She now heads to the Waterfall of Purification to heal her eyes.

9
00:02:21,626 --> 00:02:24,235
With her sight restored by the Purification Waterfall,

10
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:31,826
Sapphire sets sail for Coolland to finally face the Snow Queen.

11
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:41,640
Now, please sit back and enjoy today's episode: "The Iron Lion."

12
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,040
Sea Snake Island?

13
00:03:37,554 --> 00:03:38,800
That's Sea Snake Island.

14
00:03:42,385 --> 00:03:43,175
Father...

15
00:03:44,192 --> 00:03:45,033
Mother...

16
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:05,860
I want so badly to go to Sea Snake Island and save you.

17
00:04:07,670 --> 00:04:09,720
But what good would it do if I went now?

18
00:04:14,765 --> 00:04:19,500
Without Mephisto's power, I can't turn you back into humans.

19
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:26,300
What's more urgent is exposing the Snow Queen's plot here in Coolland...

20
00:04:27,695 --> 00:04:30,540
...and protecting Silverland as its princess.

21
00:04:31,415 --> 00:04:35,580
Until then, Father, Mother... I know you must be lonely, but please wait for me.

22
00:04:50,090 --> 00:04:51,820
Please watch over me, both of you.

23
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:55,120
Sapphire won't give up!

24
00:04:55,865 --> 00:04:58,060
She won't lose to the likes of the Snow Queen!

25
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:26,093
Now then, we'll take this as an offering for Queen Icicle.

26
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,499
If you take that, we can't do business!

27
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:39,200
Grandpa!

28
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:43,900
Get back!

29
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:45,720
Queen Icicle is waiting!

30
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,080
Move out!

31
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:56,080
"For the Snow Queen," they say!

32
00:05:58,630 --> 00:06:02,926
Morning, noon, and night, they come and seize our precious goods!

33
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,360
We're ruined!

34
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:14,120
Good morning, everyone!

35
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,466
Wow, this looks delicious!

36
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,020
How much is this?

37
00:06:21,405 --> 00:06:22,633
How much, you ask?

38
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:25,520
Then... you're not from the castle?

39
00:06:25,990 --> 00:06:27,020
No, I'm not.

40
00:06:27,515 --> 00:06:29,100
I'm the Knight of the Ribbon.

41
00:06:29,405 --> 00:06:32,240
Oh, my! Well, step right up!

42
00:06:32,265 --> 00:06:33,760
Cheapest prices around!

43
00:06:33,830 --> 00:06:36,006
The best snacks in Coolland!

44
00:06:37,574 --> 00:06:39,546
What if I were from the castle?

45
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:41,773
You see, Ribbon Knight.

46
00:06:42,565 --> 00:06:45,860
The Queen's servants never pay us.

47
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:49,360
That's why Grandpa and everyone are always struggling.

48
00:06:50,286 --> 00:06:51,420
They don't pay?

49
00:06:51,695 --> 00:06:53,006
What a terrible Queen.

50
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:59,408
Speak ill of the Queen, and those nasty soldiers will arrest you right away.

51
00:06:59,432 --> 00:07:01,807
So speaking ill of—

52
00:07:01,831 --> 00:07:02,951
Shut up!

53
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:07,660
Hey, you! You know the castle decree, don't you?

54
00:07:08,030 --> 00:07:10,720
You know what happens if you speak ill of the Queen.

55
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:12,260
P-P-Please, have mercy!

56
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,908
It was a slip of the tongue, I didn't mean it!

57
00:07:14,932 --> 00:07:15,580
Shut up!

58
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:16,073
Silence!

59
00:07:16,429 --> 00:07:18,988
We cannot change the laws of the great Coolland!

60
00:07:19,012 --> 00:07:20,359
P-Please forgive me!

61
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:22,440
Mister, you have nothing to apologize for!

62
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:24,020
What do you think you're doing?

63
00:07:24,386 --> 00:07:25,973
What? Isn't it obvious?!

64
00:07:26,486 --> 00:07:26,840
Come on!

65
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,780
The Ribbon Knight will take you on!

66
00:07:30,072 --> 00:07:31,909
Hooray! Our hero is here!

67
00:07:31,933 --> 00:07:33,980
Get those Coolland soldiers!

68
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:36,380
If you want to hear me badmouth the Queen, I'll say it!

69
00:07:36,895 --> 00:07:38,480
The Snow Queen is an idiot!

70
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:39,780
A total dimwit!

71
00:07:39,945 --> 00:07:41,660
Monster-face!

72
00:07:42,459 --> 00:07:45,613
Just because people call her the Ribbon Knight, she gets all full of herself!

73
00:07:58,553 --> 00:08:00,046
Hey, over here!

74
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:08,580
Coolland soldiers look tough, but they're so weak!

75
00:08:34,268 --> 00:08:34,795
Damn!

76
00:08:38,868 --> 00:08:39,809
Hey, get him!

77
00:08:40,079 --> 00:08:41,706
Take him, dead or alive!

78
00:09:01,719 --> 00:09:04,279
Wait!

79
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,953
Talk about an exaggeration!

80
00:09:28,649 --> 00:09:30,560
It's like an actual war!

81
00:09:35,969 --> 00:09:38,160
That's the man in the black cloak and Freeze!

82
00:09:38,990 --> 00:09:41,420
Well then, Lady Freeze, let's set the trap right away!

83
00:09:41,565 --> 00:09:42,565
I'm counting on you.

84
00:09:42,875 --> 00:09:44,820
Go back to the market immediately.

85
00:09:44,985 --> 00:09:49,246
When the Ribbon Knight returns, act natural and spy on them.

86
00:09:49,610 --> 00:09:50,280
Got it?

87
00:09:50,445 --> 00:09:51,240
Understood?

88
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:53,040
Keep a close watch on them!

89
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,200
Yes!

90
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:55,780
Lord Freeze!

91
00:09:57,660 --> 00:09:58,660
That's right!

92
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,311
That man was from the market...

93
00:10:01,436 --> 00:10:03,720
So the castle has spies even in places like that.

94
00:10:04,425 --> 00:10:06,520
That's why they find out right away whenever someone badmouths the Queen.

95
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,360
What a terrifying system.

96
00:10:11,375 --> 00:10:16,280
I can't help worrying about the Ribbon Knight's identity at such a critical time.

97
00:10:16,425 --> 00:10:19,771
That new weapon was just completed.

98
00:10:19,795 --> 00:10:20,709
A new weapon?

99
00:10:20,858 --> 00:10:22,311
Yes. So the Iron Li-...


100
00:10:23,282 --> 00:10:24,500
Keep your voice down.

101
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:27,140
I'm off to go check on it now.

102
00:10:27,819 --> 00:10:28,920
Farewell for now.

103
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:34,260
My dear henchmen, I'm counting on you.

104
00:10:35,889 --> 00:10:37,060
W-W-Who's there?!

105
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:38,860
Come on Freeze!

106
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,566
Take me to this new weapon of yours!

107
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,100
Ah, Ribbon Knight.

108
00:10:44,285 --> 00:10:45,780
You sure are quick.

109
00:10:46,139 --> 00:10:48,346
Now, follow me.

110
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,126
Wow, amazing. It's a mountain of barrels!

111
00:11:01,550 --> 00:11:03,760
That's all wine from the castle.

112
00:11:03,865 --> 00:11:05,660
I brought it from the market.

113
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:08,300
Now, the new weapon is down here.

114
00:11:27,933 --> 00:11:30,746
To think there was such a grand tunnel underground...

115
00:11:31,496 --> 00:11:33,256
Looks like it has arrived.

116
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:56,260
Wh-what is this?

117
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:57,580
This hunk of iron?

118
00:12:00,489 --> 00:12:02,140
Oh, didn't you know?

119
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:03,840
This is called an armored car.

120
00:12:03,970 --> 00:12:05,880
Come ride with me.

121
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:09,300
Are you scared?

122
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,580
Knight of the Ribbon?

123
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,306
Scared? Hardly! This will take us to the new weapon, right?

124
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:14,580
Alright, I'm getting in!

125
00:12:26,999 --> 00:12:29,720
Your face looks familiar...

126
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:32,840
Nonsense!

127
00:12:33,039 --> 00:12:34,520
I've never met anyone like you before!

128
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:54,820
This is incredible!

129
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:15,080
Tink!

130
00:13:20,461 --> 00:13:21,075
Damn it!

131
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,100
It's a dead end!

132
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:48,460
Hide!

133
00:14:14,075 --> 00:14:15,075
Hey, wait!

134
00:14:15,164 --> 00:14:16,220
Go back already!

135
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,500
Just go home!

136
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:18,860
Where did he go?

137
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:19,660
Where'd he go?

138
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:20,920
Get lost!

139
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:24,140
Haven't you found the Knight of the Ribbon yet?

140
00:14:24,165 --> 00:14:26,880
Unless he has wings, he couldn't have escaped this valley.

141
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:27,920
Search!

142
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,040
Search!

143
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:36,960
Oh, it's the Queen.

144
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:52,386
Well, well, Your Majesty.

145
00:14:52,411 --> 00:14:54,253
Welcome.

146
00:14:54,985 --> 00:14:56,840
Ah, Freeze. Good work.

147
00:14:57,275 --> 00:14:59,460
I hear the Iron Lion I've been looking forward to is complete.

148
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:01,040
May I see it right away?

149
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,813
What's the matter, Freeze?

150
00:15:05,035 --> 00:15:07,560
Bring it out and show me its invincible power.

151
00:15:08,525 --> 00:15:09,860
Right away!

152
00:15:10,225 --> 00:15:10,920
Coming, coming!

153
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:11,580
Deploy!

154
00:15:15,450 --> 00:15:18,506
I just hope the Ribbon Knight doesn't show up at the wrong time...

155
00:15:46,295 --> 00:15:49,080
What a magnificent lion form!

156
00:16:06,786 --> 00:16:08,266
Indeed. Well done, Freeze!

157
00:16:08,485 --> 00:16:11,140
And how powerful is this Iron Lion?

158
00:16:11,990 --> 00:16:14,740
Look at the hole in the lion's forehead.

159
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:20,680
Steam power shoots 100 stone arrows from it in a single blast.

160
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:21,860
A giant crossbow, then?

161
00:16:21,965 --> 00:16:24,620
It can crumble any castle wall.

162
00:16:29,829 --> 00:16:31,500
Then let us test it at once.

163
00:16:31,645 --> 00:16:32,900
Test it, you say?

164
00:16:33,275 --> 00:16:36,520
Line up the prisoners under that cliff and collapse it on them.

165
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:38,680
Just collapsing it would be boring.

166
00:16:38,855 --> 00:16:42,000
A weapon's true value is shown only when it takes human life.

167
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:45,800
So let it assist with the executions while we're at it.

168
00:16:46,225 --> 00:16:48,440
Line up the laziest ones immediately.

169
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:48,920
Yes.

170
00:16:49,375 --> 00:16:50,553
This is awful.

171
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:00,960
Tink!

172
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:03,700
Look.

173
00:17:04,139 --> 00:17:06,780
The steam is starting to vent now.

174
00:17:11,456 --> 00:17:12,456
Sapphire!

175
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,480
Where are you?

176
00:17:13,554 --> 00:17:15,155
Father in heaven!

177
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:16,613
Help me!

178
00:17:16,755 --> 00:17:18,176
Tink is going to die!

179
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:18,926
Ready!

180
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,520
Knight of the Ribbon!

181
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:32,700
Knight of the Ribbon!

182
00:17:40,379 --> 00:17:41,540
It's Sapphire!

183
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:43,479
Sapphire!

184
00:17:47,569 --> 00:17:49,306
Tink, why are you in a place like this?

185
00:17:49,409 --> 00:17:52,346
I was tricked and put on a prisoner train!

186
00:17:52,944 --> 00:17:54,359
Are you all right, Your Majesty?

187
00:17:55,054 --> 00:17:56,433
What are you waiting for?!

188
00:17:56,754 --> 00:17:58,700
Now is the time to test our iron magic!

189
00:17:59,020 --> 00:17:59,340
Fire!

190
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:00,573
Shoot the stone arrows!

191
00:18:12,024 --> 00:18:13,700
What incredible power!

192
00:18:14,004 --> 00:18:15,060
Well done, Freeze!

193
00:18:15,514 --> 00:18:18,120
That must have blown the Ribbon Knight to bits!

194
00:18:18,414 --> 00:18:21,260
I hope so... He wouldn't stand a chance!

195
00:18:21,514 --> 00:18:23,873
Curse that wretched Ribbon Knight!

196
00:18:24,419 --> 00:18:26,360
Now they know my true power!

197
00:18:39,289 --> 00:18:40,720
Soldiers, hear me!

198
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,740
Pledge your swords to me!

199
00:18:42,850 --> 00:18:45,280
Fight for the Queen of Coolland!

200
00:18:45,524 --> 00:18:47,980
My heart is always watching over you!

201
00:18:48,164 --> 00:18:49,400
To Silverland!

202
00:18:49,645 --> 00:18:51,920
Go and show them our kingdom's strength!

203
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:45,519
Halt!

204
00:19:45,919 --> 00:19:48,880
Everyone, Silverland is in sight!

205
00:19:49,329 --> 00:19:53,640
Cross this hill, and as we head down, charge all at once!

206
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:56,986
Now!

207
00:20:14,499 --> 00:20:15,740
Sapphire they're coming!

208
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:19,173
We can't let them enter Silverland!

209
00:20:22,849 --> 00:20:24,926
Father, Mother, please protect us!

210
00:20:25,284 --> 00:20:27,900
This arrow will decide the fate of Silverland!

211
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,100
Sapphire!

212
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:58,300
Freeze!

213
00:20:58,400 --> 00:20:59,100
What is happening?!

214
00:20:59,238 --> 00:21:00,320
It's turning back!

215
00:21:00,321 --> 00:21:01,860
Impossible!

216
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:02,980
What are you all doing?!

217
00:21:03,219 --> 00:21:04,300
Come on, push forward!

218
00:21:04,540 --> 00:21:05,040
Yay!

219
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:05,700
Hooray!

220
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:07,199
They're falling back!

221
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:08,600
We won!

222
00:21:08,719 --> 00:21:10,180
We beat them!

223
00:21:28,669 --> 00:21:30,619
Fall back for now!

224
00:22:09,890 --> 00:22:10,890
Tink!

225
00:22:12,027 --> 00:22:14,027
Tink!

226
00:22:14,693 --> 00:22:16,360
Tink!

227
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:19,500
Tink!

228
00:22:19,699 --> 00:22:20,760
Tink is dead!

229
00:22:21,529 --> 00:22:22,560
Tink, I'm so sorry!

230
00:22:23,024 --> 00:22:25,240
Have you already gone back to heaven?

231
00:22:25,445 --> 00:22:26,445
Sapphire!

232
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:27,880
Sapphire!

233
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:28,813
Who's there?

234
00:22:29,114 --> 00:22:30,180
Who are you?

235
00:22:31,700 --> 00:22:32,700
Hecate!

236
00:22:33,319 --> 00:22:34,440
I've been looking everywhere for you, Sapphire!

237
00:22:34,605 --> 00:22:37,040
Your mother and father are in danger!

238
00:22:37,646 --> 00:22:37,966
What?

239
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,100
In danger?

240
00:22:39,819 --> 00:22:42,979
My dad is so angry, he's going to smash the stone statues to pieces!

241
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:44,019
What?

242
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:45,400
There's nothing I can do!

243
00:22:45,569 --> 00:22:48,200
He won't calm down unless you come!

244
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:49,866
I'll go at once!

245
00:22:50,104 --> 00:22:51,340
Hecate, take me there!

246
00:22:52,279 --> 00:22:55,203
But if you go, your boy's heart will be taken...

247
00:22:55,227 --> 00:22:56,060
I'm prepared for that!

248
00:22:56,184 --> 00:22:58,573
So please guide me, Hecate!

249
00:23:00,179 --> 00:23:02,820
All right. If you insist, follow me!

250
00:23:08,719 --> 00:23:13,520
Has Tink, Sapphire's closest friend, really passed away?

251
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:19,940
What will become of Sapphire, now targeted by Mephisto and the Queen of Coolland?

252
00:23:19,964 --> 00:23:21,964

